        "original_id": "a6e575f6-bd0c-5e15-8306-c0a19dc42829",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kyosuke Himuro, Boy George, Yukinojo Mori\n- Organizations: Boøwy\n- Works: \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me\", \"Time (Clock of the Heart)\", \"Karma Chameleon\", \"Dragon Ball Z\"\n- Places: Takasaki, Gunma, Japan\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, musician, lead vocalist, DJ, fashion designer, photographer, songwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Kyosuke Himuro was born on October 7, 1960 in Takasaki, Gunma, Japan.\n- Kyosuke Himuro is a Japanese singer-songwriter and musician.\n- Boy George was born as George Alan O'Dowd on June 14, 1961.\n- Boy George is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer, and photographer.\n- Kyosuke Himuro was the lead vocalist of the rock band Boøwy from 1981 to 1988.\n- During the 1980s, Boy George's band recorded global hit songs including \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me,\" \"Time (Clock of the Heart),\" and \"Karma Chameleon.\"\n- Boy George is known for his soulful voice and androgynous appearance.\n- Yukinojo Mori has written over 2,000 songs for artists including Kyosuke Himuro, Takuro Yoshida, and Junichi Inagaki.\n- Yukinojo Mori has also written theme songs for anime series including \"Dragon Ball Z\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
